<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · sea</p><h1 class="enc-title">Sea of Japan</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as East Sea</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Sea of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/japan">Japan</a> is the marginal sea of the western Pacific between the Japanese archipelago, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sakhalin">Sakhalin</a>, the Korean Peninsula and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/russian-far-east">Russian Far East</a>. Its coasts formed the eastern edge of empires based in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/manchuria">Manchuria</a>, such as Balhae and the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/liao-dynasty">Liao</a>, and its name is disputed by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/korea">Korea</a>, which calls it the East Sea.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/sea-of-japan.jpg" alt="Sea of Japan" width="320" height="209" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Sea of Japan Map.png: Chris 73 derivative work: Phoenix7777 (talk) · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Sea_of_Japan_Map_en.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
